            <ArticleTitle>Priapism as a manifestation of tetania.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/00365590802502368</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a 40-year old male admitted because of anginal chest pain, priapism developed after coronary angiography. Chest pain and priapism most probably were due to severe hypocalcaemia 6 weeks after thyroidectomy. Both chest pain and priapism disappeared after substitution of calcium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
